From 3f35dca0a5197e1522f703ad9c17385b4676a650 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mehedi <growwithmh@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:18:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Complete authenticated member and profile workflow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The board still carried pre-auth identity habits: it asked a signed-in
person to pick themselves out of a list, and a member with no roster row
saw "Who are you?" instead of their own work. The account is the identity
now, end to end.

Identity
- ensureOwnTeamProfile() runs after the profile and site resolve, creating
  the roster row from the authenticated name. It never overwrites an
  existing profile, and reactivates one that was marked inactive.
- state.me is PB.me(). The legacy pickers are inert when Supabase is
  configured and survive only for an unconfigured local demo.
- My Work shows a setup state while the row is created and a retry on
  failure — never a fallback to the picker.

Roster lifecycle
- Removal marks the profile inactive rather than deleting it, so a task
  assigned years ago still names the right person. Rejoining reactivates.
- Assignment pickers offer active members only; historic names still
  resolve. Job title (team.body.role) is never confused with membership
  role.
- Invitations require a full name and generate a permanent board key when
  one is not supplied. The key is never derived from the email.

Interface
- The avatar menu states who you are, then My work, My profile, Manage
  people (owner/admin), Switch project (only with more than one), Sign out.
- Renaming yourself updates people.name and your own roster row together.
- The inventory editor is offered to owners and admins only, and a forced
  save explains itself instead of surfacing 42501.
- The page you were on survives a refresh, scoped per project and person.
  Board is the default, never My Work.

No schema, RLS or credential changes. 82 tests passing.

